nts><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>ADACHI KOJI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SEKI RYUICHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TANABE KOJI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TSUCHIDA KIICHIRO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>ADACHI, KOJI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SEKI, RYUICHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TANABE, KOJI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TSUCHIDA, KIICHIRO</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>Continuous production facilities for producing mechanical-structure carbon steel or alloy steel wires excellent in cold working features, which can easily realize a control rolling conventionally considered difficult with a block mill, and enables an efficient control rolling and slow cooling by effectively combining in-line the control rolling facility with a slow cooling facility, the facilities comprising, all connected continuously and sequentially, a hot rolling mill for wires, a winding device for winding rolled wires and forming them into rings, a bundling device for bundling wound wires into coils, and an inline heat treating furnace for slowly cooling the bundled, coiled wires, and using, as a final finishing mill of the hot rolling mill, a block mill preferably having a reduction of area of 25 to 60% and up to four roll stands.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne des installations de production en continu de fils d'acier de carbone ou de fils d'acier d'alliage, destinés à des structures mécaniques et possédant d'excellentes caractéristiques pour un travail à froid, ces installations pouvant facilement maîtriser le laminage considéré généralement comme difficile avec un laminoir à bloc, et permettant un laminage commandé efficace et un refroidissement lent, par combinaison efficace de l'installation de laminage en ligne avec une installation de refroidissement lent. Les installations de l'invention comprennent les éléments suivants, reliés en continu et de manière successive: un laminoir à chaud, destiné aux fils, un dispositif d'enroulement des fils laminés et de formation de ces fils en anneaux, un dispositif de groupage des fils bobinés, ainsi qu'un four de traitement thermique en ligne, destiné à refroidir lentement les fils bobinés et groupés; elles mettent en oeuvre, en tant que laminoir de finissage du laminoir à chaud, un laminoir à bloc comprenant, de préférence, une diminution de superficie de l'ordre de 25 à 60 %, et jusqu'à quatre cages de laminoir.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>